      <details class="dei-health-metric-framework"><summary>How DEI calculates and uses these health metrics</summary><div><p>DEI combines lifecycle governance, validation evidence, deployment state, scheduler/search performance, data freshness, result volume, and analyst dispositions. Metrics are decision support and require review in context.</p><dl><dt>Validation pass rate</dt><dd>Detections with passing historical validation divided by detections with an evaluated validation result.</dd><dt>Monitoring coverage</dt><dd>Enabled detections with recorded operational health evidence divided by enabled detections.</dd><dt>Review freshness</dt><dd>Detections measured within the 30-day target divided by detections with operational monitoring evidence.</dd><dt>Signal precision</dt><dd>True positives divided by true positives plus false positives. N/A means analyst classifications have not been recorded.</dd><dt>Search performance</dt><dd>Recorded search runtime and result volume. Confirm scheduler success, skipped searches, source freshness, and Job Inspector evidence in the monitoring note.</dd></dl><p>The framework follows continuous-monitoring principles from NIST SP 800-137/137A, Splunk scheduler and search-health evidence, and MITRE ATT&amp;CK Detection Strategy/Analytic separation.</p></div></details>
